==Appears==
===English Version===
*The 5th, 6th, 19th and 20th days in any month
*First appearance: September 19th, 2019 to September 20th, 2019

===Japanese Version===
*The 5rd, 6th, 19th and 20th days in any month
*First appearance: September 5th, 2019 to September 6th, 2019

==Trivia==
*Normally in the [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]] for [[:Category:Item Drop Cats#Cyclone Cats|Cyclone Cats]]  and [[:Category:Item Drop Cats#Advent Cats|Advent Cats]], the first stage is Wrath of X and the second stage is Revenge of X. However, for King Wahwah's Return, this is flipped around.
*Like [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|N-1 Grand Prix]], [[Revenge of N-1 (Merciless)|Revenge of N-1]] is likely named after the [[wikipedia:M-1 Grand Prix|M-1 Grand Prix]], the most prevalent ''[[wikipedia:Manzai|manzai]]'' competition in Japan, as [[King Wahwah]]'s Japanese description reveals him to be part of a ''manzai'' comedy duo with [[Mistress Celeboodle]]. The "N" presumably stands for ''nyan'', meaning "meow", while the "1" sounds like ''wan'', meaning "woof".
*[[Wrath of the Dogelord (Merciless)|Wrath of the Dogelord]]'s Japanese name, King of [[Doge|Wanko]] (キングオブワンコ ''Kingu obu Wanko'', "King of Doggies"), may be a reference to the annual stand-up comedy tournament [[wikipedia:ja:キングオブコント|King of Conte]] (キングオブコント ''Kingu obu Konto'').

